      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How TreeSet stores Data\n=======================",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How TreeSet stores Data\n=======================",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nbg8yPxNzlvrj4vMmstO2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 245,
      "y": 209,
      "width": 679,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1352111843,
      "version": 545,
      "versionNonce": 468524173,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789973209000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Whenever we create TreeSet object using non-paramaterized\nconstructor compareTo( ) method is called before adding elements in\nTreeSet to compare elements .\n\n2. compare() method is available in object Comaprale interface so\nwhose class object we are adding must implement comparable\ninterface .\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Whenever we create TreeSet object using non-paramaterized constructor compareTo( ) method is called before adding elements in TreeSet to compare elements .\n\n2. compare() method is available in object Comaprale interface so whose class object we are adding must implement comparable interface .\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
